ja:
二つの弱い頂点と一つの伝播関数から $\begin{aligned}\mathcal A_{\rm weak}
  &\sim g_w\,\widetilde{\Delta}_W(k)\,g_w\\
  &\sim\frac{g_w^2}{k^2+m_W^2}
  \simeq\frac{g_w^2}{m_W^2}.\end{aligned}$ が得られる。振幅を二乗すると、特定の崩壊に適した運動学的因子と相空間因子を含める前に、特徴的な抑制 $|\mathcal A_{\rm weak}|^2
  \sim\frac{g_w^4}{m_W^4},$ が生じる。弱い相互作用が核エネルギーで弱いのは、その素粒子ゲージ結合が途方もなく小さいからではなく、その媒介粒子が重いからである。

zh:
两个弱顶点和一个传播子给出 $\begin{aligned}\mathcal A_{\rm weak}
  &\sim g_w\,\widetilde{\Delta}_W(k)\,g_w\\
  &\sim\frac{g_w^2}{k^2+m_W^2}
  \simeq\frac{g_w^2}{m_W^2}.\end{aligned}$ 将振幅平方后产生特征性的压低 $|\mathcal A_{\rm weak}|^2
  \sim\frac{g_w^4}{m_W^4},$ 这是在包含特定衰变所对应的运动学和相空间因子之前。弱相互作用在核能标下之所以弱，并不是因为它的基本规范耦合小得荒谬，而是因为它的媒介粒子很重。

p.src:
Being a boson does not mean being noninteracting. Boson or fermion specifies exchange statistics; interaction vertices are separate dynamical facts. Classical light beams normally pass through one another because QED has no tree-level four-photon vertex and low-energy photon–photon scattering is extremely small. Nevertheless, two photons can interact through a virtual electron–positron loop: $\gamma+\gamma
  \longrightarrow(e^-e^+)_{\rm virtual}
  \longrightarrow\gamma+\gamma.$ When the center-of-mass energy is high enough, they may instead create a real pair, $\gamma+\gamma\longrightarrow e^-+e^+.$ Optical photons have energies of a few electron volts, while the pair threshold is of order $2m_e c^2\approx1.02\,{\rm MeV}$. The virtual process is therefore heavily suppressed at ordinary optical energies, which is why crossing light beams appear not to notice each other.

